  "body": "<!--\nThank you for contributing to the Web IDL Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n\nWhen you submit this PR, and each time you edit this comment (including checking a checkbox through the UI!), PR Preview will run and update it. As such make any edits in one go and only after PR Preview has run.\n\nIf you think your PR is ready to land, please double-check that the build is passing and the checklist is complete before pinging.\n-->\n\nThe [inherited interfaces](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#dfn-inherited-interfaces) of an interface are defined recursively: the interface it directly inherits from, plus all of *that* interface's inherited interfaces. So [inclusive inherited interfaces](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#interface-inclusive-inherited-interfaces) should walk the whole inheritance chain.\n\nBut step 3.2 advances from the fixed input |I| instead of the loop variable |interface|:\n\n> Set |interface| to the interface that |I| inherits from, if any, and null otherwise.\n\nSo after the first iteration, |interface| is always |I|'s direct parent and never becomes null. The loop never ends for any interface that inherits from another. This PR changes |I| to |interface| so each iteration moves one level up the chain.\n\nThe algorithm is used by:\n- [implements](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#implements), which regular operations and attributes use to check their `this` value\n- [internally create a new object implementing the interface](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/#internally-create-a-new-object-implementing-the-interface), which copies each ancestor's `[LegacyUnforgeable]` members onto the new instance.\n\nFor example, `CustomEvent` inherits from `Event`, which has a `[LegacyUnforgeable]` attribute:\n\n```webidl\ninterface CustomEvent : Event { ... };\n\ninterface Event {\n  ...\n  [LegacyUnforgeable] readonly attribute boolean isTrusted;\n  ...\n};\n```\n\nUnder the current text, `new CustomEvent(\"foo\")` would never finish. With the fix, it returns an object with `isTrusted` as an own property whose value is `false`.\n\nImplementations seems to behave this way. Chrome, Firefox, and Safari pass dom/idlharness.any.js on wpt.fyi, which includes test for `new CustomEvent(\"foo\")`.\n\nSo, this might be the change to align the spec with existing behavior.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/webidl/1658.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 11:03 AM UTC (a5b9ddd)\">Preview</a> | <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/webidl/1658/7b9f91b...a5b9ddd.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 10, 2026, 11:03 AM UTC (a5b9ddd)\">Diff</a>",
